      "text": "Just balances, just weights … shall ye have, Lev. 19:36. my calamity laid in the balances together, Job 6:2. Let me be weighed in an even balance, Job 31:6. to be laid in the balance, they are altogether, Ps. 62:9. false balance is abomination to the Lord, Prov. 11:1. A just weight and balance are the Lord’s, Prov. 16:11. weighed in the balances, and art found wanting, Dan. 5:27. balances of deceit are in his hand, Hosea 12:7. Shall I count them pure with the wicked balances, Micah 6:11.",
